 "verdict": "THE TABLE COLLAPSES IN THE LOCAL INFLOW: on 341 runs in mixed cells the same model costs 464.5 of deviance on the nominal rate and 436.5 on the colder body's inflow, a drop of 28.0, above the registered bar of 20.0; and the per-cell association comes out as the law predicts - positive in 9 of 11 cells where the local variable has spread (the plan's refusal rule was written with the sign the wrong way round, and that is recorded in the aggregate). The exceptions are at the largest radius: r5.9 g7 -0.132, r5.9 g9 -0.478. THE CLIFF IS NOT A SITE DRAW: the two arms' mean local inflow differs by 0.00272 in `F_local`, below the registered bar of 0.004, so both arms sat in the same medium on average and X178's 0.33 -> 0.00 stands as a property of the gap. The arms do differ in EFFECTIVE radius, though (gap 9 at r_eff 5.863, gap 10 at 5.997), because the seeding helper's rasterisation depends on the parity of SEP; the larger body is the one that did NOT fuse, so the cliff is not an artefact of that difference - it makes the observed fall conservative."
}
